{"seq":4,"slug":"governance-regulation","title":"治理与监管经济学","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/economics-finance/cryptocurrency-blockchain-economics/governance-regulation","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"dao-governance-economics","title":"DAO 治理经济学","url":"/l-doc-books/h/economics-finance/cryptocurrency-blockchain-economics/governance-regulation/dao-governance-economics","wordCount":1683,"readingTime":7},{"seq":2,"slug":"regulatory-framework-compliance","title":"监管框架与合规经济","url":"/l-doc-books/h/economics-finance/cryptocurrency-blockchain-economics/governance-regulation/regulatory-framework-compliance","wordCount":1713,"readingTime":7},{"seq":3,"slug":"cbdc-digital-currency","title":"央行数字货币经济学","url":"/l-doc-books/h/economics-finance/cryptocurrency-blockchain-economics/governance-regulation/cbdc-digital-currency","wordCount":1900,"readingTime":8}],"introMarkdown":"# 治理与监管经济学\n\n去中心化系统的治理不是无政府——它是将传统公司治理和公共选择问题搬到链上，用代币投票替代股东大会，用智能合约执行替代法律强制。本章从制度经济学和公共选择理论出发，分析三个层面的治理问题：DAO 内部的投票博弈与委托代理困境、外部监管框架对行业结构的重塑效应、以及央行数字货币作为主权回应的经济学逻辑。\n\nDAO 治理经济学探讨代币投票的寡头化倾向和搭便车问题；监管框架分析 MiCA 等立法如何改变市场准入成本和竞争格局；央行数字货币则从货币理论出发，分析 CBDC 对货币乘数、银行中介和跨境支付效率的影响。\n"}